/target
/crates/tt-firmware/target

# The pinned simulator build, fetched by `cargo xtask fetch-ttsim`.
# Not committed: a 244 KiB binary blob with its own release cadence. It is
# *pinned* in PINS.toml, which is what actually matters -- it is the oracle every
# gate is measured against.
/vendor/*.so

# Fetched by `cargo xtask gen-cfg`, pinned by SHA-256 in PINS.toml. The *generated*
# Rust table is committed; the header it came from is not.
/vendor/cfg_defines.h

# Fetched by `cargo xtask fetch-spec`, pinned by content digest in PINS.toml. The
# specification is a pinned *input*, not a dependency: it is third-party CC BY-ND
# content with its own cadence, so it is verified on arrival rather than vendored.
/vendor/tt-isa-documentation/
/vendor/tt-isa-documentation.staging/
/vendor/tt-isa-documentation.tar.gz
